  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p>Bond with a Swarm of Nature Spirits</p></blockquote><p>Feeling a deep connection to the environment, some Rangers reach out through their magical bond with the world and bind themselves to a swarm of nature spirits. The swarm becomes a potent force in battle as well as helpful company. Some Swarmkeepers are outcasts or hermits who keep to themselves and their swarms; others build vibrant communities that work for the mutual benefit of all they count as part of their swarm. The swarm might look like insects, birds, pixies, motes of light, or flowers drifting on the wind.</p><p><em>Subclass of Tasha's Cauldron of Everything, adapted to the 2024 rules by Owidyn.</em></p><h3>Swarmkeeper Features</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.classes.Item.cRFiAjbjmxRwEGcA]{Gathered Swarm}</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.classes.Item.j7dFHEWHXhva0SSb]{Swarmkeeper Magic}</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.classes.Item.ouy4QH1snz0cABig]{Writhing Tide}</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.classes.Item.UHgCecDragTxj9Gn]{Mighty Swarm}</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.classes.Item.2ORbqPTN1F7tBGC6]{Swarming Dispersal}</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Swarmkeeper Spells</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Ranger Level</th><th>Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplFaerieFire]{Faerie Fire}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMageHand00]{Mage Hand}</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWeb0000000]{Web}</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplGaseousFor]{Gaseous Form}</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplArcaneEye0]{Arcane Eye}</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplInsectPlag]{Insect Plague}</td></tr></tbody></table>",
